Implement CGDisplayIsOnline, which Qt needs before it can open its platform plugin.

Found by staging a QT application, CMake.app, which is the first non Cocoa, non cocotron, non
wxWidgets toolkit this port has run. Qt reaches CoreGraphics through its own cocoa plugin, and
that plugin refused to load:

    Symbol not found: _CGDisplayIsOnline
      Referenced from: /Applications/CMake.app/Contents/PlugIns/platforms/libqcocoa.dylib
      Expected in: /System/Library/Frameworks/CoreGraphics.framework/Versions/A/CoreGraphics

CGDirectDisplay.m already had the three sibling predicates, IsCaptured, IsInMirrorSet and IsMain,
and CGGetOnlineDisplayList right above them, which enumerates [display screens] and numbers them
from 1. So online means exactly what that enumeration means and the answer is derived from the
same place rather than hardcoded: a display is online if it is one of the screens.

Not a stub. CGDisplayIsInMirrorSet a few lines up prints STUB and returns FALSE, and a stub here
would answer the same for a display that IS online, which is a wrong answer rather than a missing
one.

--- a/CoreGraphics/CGDirectDisplay.m
+++ b/CoreGraphics/CGDirectDisplay.m
@@ -261,6 +261,15 @@
     return display == 1;
 }
 
+// Numbered from 1, the same way CGGetOnlineDisplayList above enumerates [display screens].
+boolean_t CGDisplayIsOnline(CGDirectDisplayID display) {
+    NSDisplay *current = currentDisplay();
+    if (!current)
+        return FALSE;
+
+    return display >= 1 && display <= [[current screens] count];
+}
+
